=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client data port, also Microsoft.UI-free),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view).
- Data sources — the web page's two hooks, each ported to the generated OpenAPI client (ADR-004):
  * useMediaLatest → GET /media/latest?vehicle_id={id} (operation get_api_v1_media_latest): the PRIMARY read;
    its presence/failure drives the now-playing card + the volume gauge and the page success/error branch.
    Parsed into MediaReading (Model.cs MediaReading.FromJson; now_playing_title/artist/album/station,
    playback_source/status, now_playing_duration/elapsed ms, audio_volume/_max/_increment — snake_case, null-
    tolerant). Field names reuse the proven wire shape of the sibling MediaNowPlayingWidget.
  * useMediaHistory → GET /media?vehicle_id={id}&limit=500 (operation get_api_v1_media): the SECONDARY best-
    effort read feeding the four stat tiles, the volume-over-time area chart, the source-distribution pie and
    the history table; a transport failure degrades to no rows (MediaPlayerClientFeed.FetchHistoryAsync catches
    ApiException → empty), mirroring the web's two independent queries (only latestError reaches the web
    PageContainer; historyError is an inline banner over a still-rendered card). Parsed by
    MediaHistoryEntry.ParseList → MediaHistoryEntry.FromJson.
- Projection (MediaPlayerProjection.Project) is the 1:1 port of the web render body + its statusVariant /
  statusLabel / sourceIcon / fmtPlayTime helpers and the stats / volumeChartData / sourceData memos. State
  precedence mirrors the web data lifecycle (loading → error → empty → success); empty = no now-playing object
  AND no history (nothing to render), so the page is never blank (engineering guideline #6).
- Units (P1/S5): audio volume is a raw device scale (0..max), NOT an SI quantity, so there is no unit
  conversion on this surface; m:ss play-clocks come from millisecond positions via fmtPlayTime parity
  (MediaPlayerProjection.PlayClock). Nothing non-SI is stored or computed.
- Nav: route name MediaPlayer → path media-player already exists in RouteTable.cs#280 (RouteGroup.VehicleSystems);
  the page factory is registered in Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs ("MediaPlayer" → new
  FeatureViews.VehicleSystems.MediaPlayerPage()).
- Catalog: 11 of the 26 web i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw
  (translation.* prefix: Artist, Paused, Playing, Source, Status, Stopped, Time, Track, Volume,
  error.loadFailed, records); the 15 missing natural-language keys were ADDED to all three locales (Avg Volume,
  Media Player, No playback history, No playback history for this period, No source data available, No track,
  No volume data for this period, Now playing volume and listening history, Playback History, Source
  Distribution, Top Source, Unique Tracks, Unknown artist, Volume Step, Volume over Time). Every visible literal
  resolves through ILocalizer with the web key names; resolved once in MediaStrings.Resolve (Model.cs).

